From: System Electronics
Date: Tue, 9 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] medialib: carry sensor_id into the GStreamer-mode profile

In GStreamer mode there is no medialib profile file: ConfigManagerInteractor
::create_dummy_profile_interactor() synthesises one from the frontend config
through config_profile_t::from_frontend_config().

That conversion copies resolution, format, zoom, rotation, flip, hailort,
analytics, stabilizer and IQ settings, but never copies the sensor index. The
frontend schema does accept "sensor_id" under "input_video", the parser stores
it in frontend_config.input_config.sensor_index, and several call sites use it
(get_sensor_mode_info_sdr/hdr, get_raw_capture_path, get_pixel_format). But
IspManager::init_isp_out_device() reads it back from the profile:

    size_t sensor_index = current_profile_opt.value()->sensor_config.input_video.sensor_id;

which stays at its SENSOR_0 default. On Astrial H15 the only camera sits on
CSI-RX1, so SensorRegistry then looks for a sensor behind cdns_csi2rx_0, finds
none, and the pipeline dies with "No enabled remote source connected to
cdns_csi2rx_0" followed by "Failed to set IMX_WDR".

The reverse conversion, to_frontend_config(), already carries the field:

    .sensor_index = static_cast<size_t>(sensor_config.input_video.sensor_id)

so this only restores the missing symmetry.

Note: source and source_type show the same asymmetry and are also dropped by
from_frontend_config(). Left alone here, nothing needs them yet.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
--- a/hailo-media-library/media_library/include/media_library/media_library_types.hpp
+++ b/hailo-media-library/media_library/include/media_library/media_library_types.hpp
@@ -2003,6 +2003,8 @@
     void from_frontend_config(const frontend_config_t &frontend_config)
     {
         // Convert sensor config
+        sensor_config.input_video.sensor_id =
+            static_cast<sensor_id_t>(frontend_config.input_config.sensor_index);
         sensor_config.input_video.resolution.width =
             frontend_config.input_config.resolution.dimensions.destination_width;
         sensor_config.input_video.resolution.height =
